From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PickleHik3 <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] meson: options for the panels a build can compile out

New options, all true, which is upstream's build: welcome-panel, lang-panel, alerts-panel,
lockscreen-panel, osk-panel, convergence-panel, sensors-panel, features-panel, updates-panel
and about-panel, and plugins and tests for the device plugins and the tests. A panel that is off
has no dependency (accountsservice and polkit for the language panel, libcellbroadcast for the
alerts panel, libpms for the language, OSK and OS update panels), no source files, defines
MOBILE_SETTINGS_HAVE_<PANEL>_PANEL as 0 in mobile-settings-config.h and takes its objects out of
the GtkBuilder file and the resource file that name them (tools/tl-ui-filter, between
'<!-- tl-if PANEL -->' markers). libnm is needed only with gcc-panels, which it was written
for. The overview, quick settings (top bar), compositor and feedback panels are always built.
The markers and C guards follow, one commit per panel.
---

